{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And YHWH Elohim planted a garden in Eden.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): Scripture ascribes the planting to the Name, may He be exalted, to explain that it is 'the planting of YHWH' — not that He brought trees from another place and planted them there, but rather they were His plantings, the work of His hands, for His glory. And so King David, peace be upon him, called them 'trees of YHWH,' as it is written (Psalms 104:16): ״ישבעו עצי ה' ארזי לבנון אשר נטע״. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: ישבעו — they are sated with their life; חייהם — they are sated with their waters; ישבעו מטעתן — they are sated with their planting. They need no irrigation, no tending, no pruning; for were it not so, from the day Adam was driven out from there, who tended it and who watered them and who attended to them? Rather, they are in the manner of what is written (Ezekiel 47:12): ״לא יבול עלהו ולא יתם פריו כי מימיו מן המקדש המה יוצאים״. And He mentioned מן המזרח ('from the east'), and thereby Scripture informs us of the virtue of the eastern wind, for the Garden of Eden was planted there. Know that the choicest fruits are in the east, as it is written (Deuteronomy 33): ״וממגד תבואות שמש״. And so our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: an eastern wind settles the mind and strengthens the power and fortifies the heart, for the air in it is superior beyond all. And upon this it says: וישם שם את האדם אשר יצר — 'and He placed there the man whom He had formed.'" "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'And YHWH Elohim planted a garden in Eden מקדם' — its meaning is that He had already planted it, and the intent is not that He planted it now; for if so, it would have been fitting to say, 'Let there be trees in the Garden of Eden,' just as throughout the six days of Creation 'Let there be such-and-such' is said by command, or that it should say, תדשא הארץ עדן. And furthermore, who mentioned Eden to us until now, that Scripture should say that the Holy One, blessed be He, planted a garden in Eden? Rather, this planting of Eden was already alluded to in the verse בראשית, as I hinted there. And the meaning of מקדם is: before the world was created. According to this, וישם שם את האדם אשר יצר — 'He had already placed there the man whom He formed' — from the source of wisdom. And you should know that the pure souls come from the east, and this is what our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted in the Book of the Bahir: 'From the east of the world the seed comes to Israel,' for the spinal cord is drawn from the brain of man and comes to his member, and from there is the seed, as it is written (Isaiah 43:5): ״ממזרח אביא זרעך״ — when Israel is good, from this place 'I bring your seed,' and new seed is renewed for you; and when Israel is wicked, they come from seed that has already come into the world, as it is written (Ecclesiastes 1:4): ״דור הולך ודור בא״ — this teaches that it has already come. And what is 'from the west I gather you'? From that attribute which always inclines toward the west. And why is it called מערב (west)? Because there all the seed מתערב (intermingles). The explanation of this Midrash, in my opinion: the attribute of the east is Tiferet, which is the middle line, and from there the souls come to the Foundation of the world, called Covenant; therefore it says 'and it comes to his member,' and from there is the seed. And the attribute of the west is the Crown (Atarah), and this is what it says: the Shekhinah is in the west. And just as the seed is drawn from the brain through the spinal cord and comes to the member, so too the soul is drawn from Repentance (Teshuvah) through the middle line, which is the east of the world, and comes through the west. And in my opinion it was to this matter that Isaiah, peace be upon him, alluded when he said (Isaiah 48:1): ״שמעו זאת בית יעקב הנקראים בשם ישראל וממי יהודה יצאו״ — that is, from the seed of Judah — and he mentioned Judah because his banner was in the east. And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:09:28.006530487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}